WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:06.880
Sony just made their biggest change in history.
From 2028, there will be no more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:11.360
physical PlayStation games.
Everything will be digital.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:17.200
No more secondhand, no more sharing games,&nbsp;
everything will be through the Sony store.&nbsp;

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:21.520
And it’s backfiring.
But according to Sony,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:27.440
this is just where customers are moving.
So, are they right? Is this really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:41.440
just where things are moving?
And, why are physical games still so important?

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.760
Let’s take a closer look at what’s&nbsp;
really happening, and Sony’s claims.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:51.440
In the official blog post, they say “As consumer&nbsp;
preferences and the broader entertainment industry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.400
continue to shift away from physical discs to&nbsp;
digital, physical game disc production for all new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:02.240
games releasing on PlayStation consoles will be&nbsp;
discontinued starting January 2028. Following this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:08.320
date, new games will be available on PlayStation&nbsp;
Store and at retailers in digital formats only.”&nbsp;

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:13.120
This is a first in PlayStation history.
This also seems to heavily imply,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:19.120
the PS6 won’t have a disc drive. So&nbsp;
no more Blu-ray or DVD support either.&nbsp;

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:24.960
Immediately, after this announcement went&nbsp;
live, the backlash was widespread, and intense.&nbsp;

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:31.200
66 thousand likes, over 100 thousand replies,&nbsp;
70 thousand retweets. Almost twice the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:38.080
amount of replies to likes, is a bad sign.
“You will own nothing”. 122 thousand likes.&nbsp;

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:47.200
“#NOTBUYINGPS6 unless it supports physical games.”
“Guys, this is a really bad decision. Wtf.”&nbsp;

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:52.160
“I have no words, final nail in the&nbsp;
coffin of the company I once loved.”&nbsp;

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:57.680
This news began spreading everywhere.
Retailers, understandably, weren’t very happy.&nbsp;

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:02.960
“Shall we start with PS+ cancellations for today?”
Which, for the record, people did.&nbsp;

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:08.400
Other brands began mocking Sony’s announcement.
“In response to trends in the gaming industry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:14.320
Domino’s will cease production of physical pizzas&nbsp;
and shift to production of digital pizzas only”.&nbsp;

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:17.760
KFC did the same.
Some of these were pretty funny.&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:21.840
“In response to the gaming industry removing&nbsp;
physical offerings, [Proton] have decided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:26.720
to make our services entirely physical.”
It wasn’t just Sony getting flack either.&nbsp;

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:30.160
They get paid to promote&nbsp;
upcoming games with posts on X.&nbsp;

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.240
But even the games affiliated with Sony,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:36.480
after the announcement, received&nbsp;
huge backlash, and review bombs.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.000
What makes all of this even more ironic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:12.000
is that Sony made fun of Xbox for doing&nbsp;
this same thing, except 13 years ago.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:23.840
Boy does this ad have a lot more attention today.
“This video has aged just as well as Netflix's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:28.400
"Love is sharing a password" tweet”
“Play does have LIMITS after all.”&nbsp;

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:34.560
But, this ad shows us how Sony have changed.
This is Shuhei Yoshida and Adam Boyes. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:40.080
former President of Sony Worldwide Studios and&nbsp;
former VP of Third-Party / Publisher &amp; Developer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:45.040
Relations, and was heavily involved&nbsp;
in some of the biggest Sony titles.&nbsp;

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:50.880
But Yoshida was actually fired, because he&nbsp;
disagreed with PlayStation CEO Jim Ryan.&nbsp;

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:56.080
“Jim Ryan wanted to remove me from first-party&nbsp;
because I didn't listen to him. He asked to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.080 --> 00:04:01.040
some ridiculous things, and I said 'No.'”
The point about first party developers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:05.840
is very interesting, because it’s&nbsp;
not just consumers who are upset.&nbsp;

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:12.000
Industry veterans and long-time Sony partners, are&nbsp;
expressing that they’re not thrilled about this.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.624
Hideo Kojima, one of the most acclaimed&nbsp;
video game directors in history, said&nbsp;

00:04:16.624 --> 00:04:22.720
[Hideo Kojima]: Since production is ending in&nbsp;
2028, this is about video games, but I grew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:28.320
up with physical media, so I find it really&nbsp;
sad. They are downloaded to the hard drive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:33.360
that means the game data remains on your own&nbsp;
hardware. However, if things shift to streaming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:38.800
in the future, that won’t be the case anymore.
There are companies that own these servers and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:43.840
let you 'turn the tap' for a monthly fee.&nbsp;
However, one naturally has to consider the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:49.520
possibility that if there is a change, the&nbsp;
data inside will stop being distributed.&nbsp;

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:55.360
And if that happens you won’t be able to&nbsp;
watch or play the movies and games you like.&nbsp;

00:04:55.360 --> 00:05:01.360
But, something about all of this is a bit weird.
On July 3, two days after the announcement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:06.640
Sony CEO Hiroki Totoki sold 56%&nbsp;
of his SONY shares for $4.7M.&nbsp;

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:11.520
On the same day, Chairman Kenichiro&nbsp;
Yoshida sold 400,000 shares,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:16.160
and other Sony executives sold too.
The combined insider sales are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:20.480
roughly around $10.5 million.
Granted, this is related to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:29.360
Sony buyback. But the timing sure is strange.
But, despite all the backlash… is Sony wrong?&nbsp;

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:35.200
Is this just the uncomfortable&nbsp;
truth, that physical games are dying?

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:46.640
Sony said “consumer preferences and the broader&nbsp;
entertainment industry continue to shift away from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:50.560
physical discs to digital”. So, are they right?
Tension&nbsp;

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:56.720
According to Sony, 78% of games sold&nbsp;
for the full year of 2025, were digital.&nbsp;

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:04.560
But in Q4 digital downloads for full games&nbsp;
was 85% of sales, while physical was just 15%.&nbsp;

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:08.880
But, that’s just Sony, and there’s&nbsp;
something else to consider.&nbsp;

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:14.480
On the PS store are hundreds of games, many&nbsp;
of which never make it to physical media,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:20.560
because their market is so small anyway. It’s the&nbsp;
bigger games that have wider, physical releases.&nbsp;

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:25.360
Since Sony is including everything, this&nbsp;
will be naturally skewed more digital.&nbsp;

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:29.040
A heavy-hitting physical game, like&nbsp;
God of War, will be counted the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:34.560
as a 99 cent game on the PS store.
But, only 7 games have sold over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:39.120
100,000 physical units for the financial year.&nbsp;
Which makes it clear how small the library of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:44.400
physical games is on the PS5, compared&nbsp;
to the PS4, which had a vast library.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:50.800
Though, even the biggest physical releases&nbsp;
were heavily skewed towards digital. FC 26,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:57.200
aka the new name for the FIFA series, had&nbsp;
physical sales of just 12%. Not only that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:03.440
6.4 million didn’t even buy the game, at all,&nbsp;
but played it through the PS Plus subscription.&nbsp;

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:08.080
Other games had a larger physical&nbsp;
split, but not too much more.&nbsp;

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:11.520
Resident Evil Requiem, 3.5 million sales,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:18.160
about 28% physical, Crimson Desert,&nbsp;
1.9 million, about 20% physical.&nbsp;

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:22.320
And this gets a bit more bleak when&nbsp;
we look at the actual financials.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:27.680
According to their financial results for&nbsp;
2025, physical software, aka physical games,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:34.480
was 121 billion yen. Digital&nbsp;
software was 949 billion yen.&nbsp;

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:39.760
But, let’s look a bit further, beyond Sony.
According to the UK digital entertainment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:46.080
and retail association, 89.5% of games&nbsp;
sold in the UK, were digital downloads.&nbsp;

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:53.600
Though note, this includes mobile apps,&nbsp;
though that only made up 30% of sales.&nbsp;

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:59.280
It seems, to be honest, pretty cut and dry.
Physical, is without a doubt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:05.520
becoming more niche for video games.
Though, there is one hole in Sony’s argument.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:11.120
You can buy a regular PS5, or a digital-only&nbsp;
version, which has no disc drive.&nbsp;

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:15.840
“Not only does the company charge less&nbsp;
for the digital-only PS5, but the new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:23.760
PS5 Pro only comes in a digital version.”
Yet, 82% of all PS5s have a disc drive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:28.960
Even though it’s more expensive, and&nbsp;
even though most sales are digital.&nbsp;

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:31.920
That tells you something&nbsp;
about what customers want.&nbsp;

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:36.560
They still value having&nbsp;
both, and will pay for both.&nbsp;

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:39.920
So, why is Sony doing this… really.&nbsp;

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:52.400
It turns out, it’s because&nbsp;
of “consumer preferences”.

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:58.400
If you’ve watched this far, you probably enjoy&nbsp;
our stuff, so consider subscribing! Thanks.

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:03.280
Rhys Elliott, from Alinea&nbsp;
Analytics made an excellent point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:07.040
about something Sony is really fighting.
[Rhys Elliott, Alinea Analytics]: “Our estimates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:15.440
have 25%, almost 900K players of Resident Evil&nbsp;
Requiem’s PS5 player base clocking under 10 hours.&nbsp;

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:19.760
What I’m getting at here is that plenty&nbsp;
of those physical copies will end up in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:25.360
the hands of resellers, which is exactly&nbsp;
what neither Capcom nor PlayStation wants.”

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:29.280
The beauty of physical products, is&nbsp;
that you can sell them, loan them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:33.840
or give them away when you’re done.
But, every time someone does this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:39.120
it means Sony misses out on revenue.
The reality is, Sony aren’t doing this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:44.480
because of “consumer trends”. They’re doing&nbsp;
this, to improve margins, gain sales that are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:48.560
taken by second hand copies.
This is all about margins.&nbsp;

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:53.040
With the move away from physical disc, no&nbsp;
more second hand games bought and sold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:56.080
no more sharing games.
You can’t even buy a console&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.080 --> 00:10:00.400
second hand with games, because they’re&nbsp;
attached to the account, not the console.&nbsp;

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:05.440
Everything you buy will be under Sony’s&nbsp;
thumb, and they can do whatever they want.&nbsp;

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:11.440
They just removed over 500 movies from the&nbsp;
PlayStation store as licenses expire. Even if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:17.360
you bought some of these, you can’t watch them&nbsp;
anymore. And they can do this with games too.&nbsp;

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:22.080
In fact, they just did in&nbsp;
August, removing 9 from PS Plus.&nbsp;

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:26.320
Also, under their terms, if you&nbsp;
haven’t used your account in 3 years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:31.760
they’ll just close your account, and you’ll lose&nbsp;
permanent access to all products you paid for.&nbsp;

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:37.680
As a reminder, people pay over $600 for&nbsp;
one of these consoles. Imagine doing that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:42.560
and paying hundreds more for digital&nbsp;
products, and Sony removes them all.&nbsp;

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:47.680
And if you don’t believe me, game&nbsp;
companies are already doing this.

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:55.200
In 2024 Ubisoft, another game publisher, delisted&nbsp;
the open-world multiplayer racing game “The Crew”.&nbsp;

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:58.240
They then shut the game servers&nbsp;
down, meaning nobody could play&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:04.000
it anymore, because it’s “always online”.
Customers had paid full price for this game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:08.400
and had also purchased microtransactions.
[Ubisoft]: "We understand this may be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:11.360
disappointing for players still enjoying the game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:16.480
but it has become a necessity due to upcoming&nbsp;
server infrastructure and licensing constraints.”&nbsp;

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:20.720
Customers were, understandably, quite&nbsp;
annoyed, which led to a lawsuit.&nbsp;

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:25.120
Ubisoft argued that there was no reason&nbsp;
for players to believe they were purchasing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:29.760
“unfettered ownership rights in the game.”
This is why the “Stop Killing Games”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:36.160
movement has gained so much support in the EU.
Even if people don’t buy physical games as much,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:42.880
they still like the option to be able to.
Hence the massive proportion of disc-drive PS5s.&nbsp;

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:48.320
Sony is just taking away choice from consumers.
Choice that other companies… hopefully…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:52.800
will continue to offer. Which&nbsp;
makes the PS5 less appealing.

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:57.680
One of the best feelings, is playing an&nbsp;
old, favourite game, or movie from 10,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.680 --> 00:12:02.400
20, or even 30 years ago, because&nbsp;
you still have the physical disc.&nbsp;

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:08.560
No need to worry about licenses expiring, accounts&nbsp;
being removed, online support disappearing.&nbsp;

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:13.920
Push it in and play, because it’s your&nbsp;
property, which you exchanged money for.&nbsp;

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:19.280
The scariest part, about all of this,&nbsp;
is that it might be a thing of the past.&nbsp;

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:24.320
You won’t be able to share games, or sell them, or&nbsp;
trade them in. They’ll be locked to one account,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:29.120
which is at the mercy of Sony.
If their license ends, gone. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:35.040
you get banned, even for a false reason, gone.
Sony can’t take your physical products from you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:38.240
but they can do whatever they&nbsp;
want with your digital ones.&nbsp;

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:42.480
[Hideo Kojima, 2021]: “Eventually, even digital&nbsp;
data will no longer be owned by individuals on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:47.120
their own initiative. Whenever there is&nbsp;
a major change or accident in the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:54.080
in a country, in a government, in an idea, in&nbsp;
a trend, access to it may suddenly be cut off.”

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:57.440
But there’s another major&nbsp;
problem with digital games.&nbsp;

00:12:57.440 --> 00:13:00.880
Physical prices fluctuate with supply and demand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:05.360
but for Digital, Sony controls&nbsp;
the store, and the price.&nbsp;

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:10.000
They can also determine what price&nbsp;
you pay, vs what your friend pays.&nbsp;

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:14.240
And recently, people discovered&nbsp;
a massive experiment, where Sony&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:25.120
quietly did exactly this. (Also show this).
